    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0518" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg404"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Prime Minister Churchill to President Roosevelt
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d189-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-29">29 July 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Former Naval Person to President. Personal and
                    most secret. No. 387.</p>
                <p>I was so glad to hear your voice again<anchor n="2" xml:id="d189-f2"/> and that
                    you were in such good spirits, and also that you like our plans for “<hi rendition="#small-caps">Quadrant</hi>” to
                    which we are all ardently looking forward.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d189-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d189-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d189-f1-content">
                <p>Channel of transmission not indicated. An information copy of this message was
                    sent to Hull by the British Minister at Washington (Campbell) on July 30, 1943
                    (740.0011 EW/7–3043).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d189-f2" n="2" xml:id="d189-f2-content">
                <p>The reference is probably to Roosevelt’s broadcast of July 28, 1943. See
                    Rosenman, <ref target="#pg326">pp. 326</ref>–<ref target="#pg336">336</ref>;
                    Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, vol. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">ix</hi>, July 31, 1943, pp. 57–62.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d189-f3" n="3" xml:id="d189-f3-content">
                <p>For the full text of this message, see <ref target="frus1943v02#pg_336">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1943, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, pp. 336</ref>–<ref
                        target="frus1943v02#pg_337">337</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
